description: LocalAgent project rules (pure-PyTorch <100M tool-calling agent)
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---
Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root — it is the source of truth for setup, build/test commands, and
conventions (shared with Claude Code and Codex). Key rules:

- Pure PyTorch only. Do NOT add `transformers`, `trl`, `deepspeed`, or other training frameworks.
- Three model tiers under `configs/model/` (ultra-tiny ~1M byte-level, tiny ~30M, small ~90M).
  Every config must pass `ModelConfig.assert_within_budget()` (<100M). Never bypass it.
- One data interchange format: `localagent.data.schema.Conversation`. Don't invent ad-hoc dicts.
- Synthetic data targets are canonical (sorted-key compact JSON); train/eval slot pools are
  disjoint. Preserve both.
- Honest stubs: unimplemented code raises `NotImplementedError("TODO(phase-N): …")`. Report real
  eval numbers; never fake 100%.
- Before finishing: `pytest -q` green, `ruff check src tests` clean. Don't commit `runs/`,
  checkpoints, or `*.png`.

Quick signal: `python scripts/flywheel.py --quick`. Perf: `python scripts/benchmark.py`.
